Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their possible use & key filter ideas  
• alien_data."state": groups aliens by U.S. state; lets us find the 10 states with the largest alien‐population.  
• alien_data."aggressive": 0 = friendly, 1 = hostile; used to count friendly vs hostile aliens and to compare the two totals.  
• alien_data."age": needed to calculate the average age per state and to keep only states whose average age > 200 years.

Core logic / conditions to apply  
1. Build a population table per state (COUNT *).  
2. Take the 10 states with the largest counts (ORDER BY COUNT DESC LIMIT 10).  
3. For those 10 states calculate  
   • friendly = SUM(CASE WHEN aggressive = 0 THEN 1 END)  
   • hostile  = SUM(CASE WHEN aggressive = 1 THEN 1 END)  
   • avg_age  = AVG(age)  
4. Keep rows where friendly > hostile AND avg_age > 200.  
5. Finally, COUNT(*) of the remaining rows answers the question.

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries – from simple inspection to the final answer.  
(All tables/columns are wrapped in double quotes to stay SQLite‑safe; each query is capped with LIMIT 20 where appropriate.)

```sql
-- 1. List distinct state names appearing in alien_data
SELECT DISTINCT "state"
FROM "alien_data"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Alien population by state (top 20)
SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
       COUNT(*)        AS alien_count
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
ORDER  BY alien_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Top‑10 states by alien population
SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
       COUNT(*)        AS alien_count
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
ORDER  BY alien_count DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

```sql
-- 4. Friendly vs. hostile counts for each state
SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS friendly_count,
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS hostile_count
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
ORDER  BY friendly_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Average alien age per state (only >200 yrs shown)
SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
       AVG("age")      AS avg_age
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
HAVING AVG("age") > 200
ORDER  BY avg_age DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. States where friendly outnumber hostile and average age >200
SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS friendly_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS hostile_cnt,
       AVG("age")                                        AS avg_age
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
HAVING SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) >
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
   AND AVG("age") > 200
ORDER  BY friendly_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Build a CTE that keeps only the top‑10 states by population
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
         COUNT(*)        AS total
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
  ORDER  BY total DESC
  LIMIT 10
)
SELECT * FROM pop;
```

```sql
-- 8. Join the top‑10 states with detailed friendly / hostile / age stats
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
         COUNT(*)        AS total
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
  ORDER  BY total DESC
  LIMIT 10
)
SELECT p.state,
       SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS friendly,
       SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS hostile,
       AVG(a."age")                                        AS avg_age
FROM   pop AS p
JOIN   "alien_data" AS a
       ON LOWER(a."state") = p.state
GROUP  BY p.state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. From the previous join, keep only states meeting the friendliness & age criteria
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
         COUNT(*)        AS total
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
  ORDER  BY total DESC
  LIMIT 10
),
agg AS (
  SELECT p.state,
         SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS friendly,
         SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS hostile,
         AVG(a."age")                                        AS avg_age
  FROM   pop AS p
  JOIN   "alien_data" AS a
         ON LOWER(a."state") = p.state
  GROUP  BY p.state
)
SELECT *
FROM   agg
WHERE  friendly > hostile
  AND  avg_age  > 200
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER – how many of the top‑10 states satisfy both conditions?
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT LOWER("state") AS state,
         COUNT(*)        AS total
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY LOWER("state")
  ORDER  BY total DESC
  LIMIT 10
),
agg AS (
  SELECT p.state,
         SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS friendly,
         SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS hostile,
         AVG(a."age")                                        AS avg_age
  FROM   pop AS p
  JOIN   "alien_data" AS a
         ON LOWER(a."state") = p.state
  GROUP  BY p.state
)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS num_states
FROM   agg
WHERE  friendly > hostile
  AND  avg_age  > 200;
```

